Step to create Docker Image
Step 1: Download WSL2 on Window PC and install Docker Window
Step 2: Use Git Bash Command Line to run: docker run -it --rm python:3.8.12-slim. This will create an image with python 3.8 version with docker.
Step 3: Build an image using Docker file: docker build -t zoomcamp-test . 
        Replace zoomcamp-test with the image name
        To access the image, now run: docker run -it --rm zoomcamp-test:latest
Step 4: Expose the port from the VM to the currnt machine and map the port from docker img to the host machine